From dc235b48fc41a6ab774c561d77ebedbf6a920e83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kostersitz <mkostersitz@mac.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:25:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Allow the Surface Duo com.microsoft.device boot jar package

check_boot_jars rejects packages that are not on the allow list; DUO-DE adds a clean-room com.microsoft.device boot jar
(com.microsoft.device.display.DisplayMask) like the stock Surface Duo firmware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I2d81fe86029ed3c26f6f7d6b5285bd6601c675ac
---
 scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt b/scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt
index 38c72b8b3..0a2177e30 100644
--- a/scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt
+++ b/scripts/check_boot_jars/package_allowed_list.txt
@@ -268,3 +268,6 @@ org\.chromium\.arc\..*
 # Packages used for wear-sdk in Wear OS
 com\.google\.wear
 com\.google\.wear\..*
+###################################################
+# Surface Duo (DUO-DE): clean-room com.microsoft.device boot jar
+com\.microsoft\.device\.display
-- 
2.43.0

